<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila's PHIBOR mixed ahead of T-bill auction.</title>
<headline>Manila's PHIBOR mixed ahead of T-bill auction.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine interbank offered rates (PHIBOR) were mixed as long-term rates nudged higher and short-term rates slipped, traders said.</p>
<p>&quot;The rates are just following their spot rates,&quot; one trader said.</p>
<p>Short-term rates slipped following the rate cut in the Central Bank's overnight rates.</p>
<p>Long-term rates were firmer as bankers were divided over the direction of Treasury bill rates at Monday's auction.  </p>
<p>Average rates quoted by 20 banks were:</p>
<p>			 JUNE 13		 JUNE 11</p>
<p>    1 W		12  5/16		12  9/16</p>
<p>    2 W		12  1/8		 12  1/4</p>
<p>    1 M		11  3/8		 11  1/2</p>
<p>    2 M		11  3/8		 11  7/16</p>
<p>    3 M		11  7/16		11  3/8</p>
<p>    6 M		11  7/16		11  1/4</p>
<p>    12M		11  3/8		 11  1/4</p>
<p>    VAL		16-Jun		  13-Jun</p>
